Lines that do not parse among lines that do (issue #351). A line end gets
its `;` only while the code since the last terminator parses: `nCount :=
1` is still terminated, but the raw `delete from` line is not, nor is
anything after it up to the `;` the source wrote, so that run stays one
unexpected_token. The unparsed line keeps its source indentation and
spacing; the parsed lines around it, including the :IF block it sits in,
are formatted as usual. A malformed statement that is whole
(`nTotal := nCount +* 2;`) is not a run the formatter could not
delimit, so it is still normalized.
-- input.ssl --
:DECLARE nCount, nTotal, bReady;
nCount := 1
:IF bReady;
  delete  from STAGING   where ID = 1
    nTotal := nCount;
:ENDIF;
nTotal :=   nCount +* 2;
-- format --
:DECLARE nCount, nTotal, bReady;

nCount := 1;

:IF bReady;
  delete  from STAGING   where ID = 1
	nTotal := nCount;
:ENDIF;

nTotal := nCount + * 2;
-- diagnostics --
3:1-3:4 error unexpected_token: Unexpected keyword ':IF' - expected an operator or ';' (is the previous statement missing its ';'?)
4:11-4:15 error unexpected_token: Unexpected identifier 'from' - expected an operator or ';'
7:21-7:22 error unexpected_token: Unexpected operator '*' - expected an expression
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
3:1-3:4 error unexpected_token: Unexpected keyword ':IF' - expected an operator or ';' (is the previous statement missing its ';'?)
4:11-4:15 error unexpected_token: Unexpected identifier 'from' - expected an operator or ';'
7:21-7:22 error unexpected_token: Unexpected operator '*' - expected an expression
